claimed: intent-domain-in-names — test the hypothesis the last two lanes left standing: that the case NAMES carry the domain or nothing does. A taxonomy of Proposal/Request/Notification with a bare what:String never says its subject is meetings, so a refund request reads as a Request honestly rather than mistakenly. Same 120-message fixture, same best configuration, three arms: generic names with examples and no gate, domain-bearing names with examples and no gate, and domain-bearing names with the gate on top. If the names alone lift Other, the fix belongs in the TYPE and the gate is a workaround for an unnamed domain; if they do not, the gate is doing real work the type cannot do, and that is worth knowing before more prompt machinery is built. Labels are mapped back to the canonical class names so the two taxonomies are scored on one axis.
